# Reduced repro for the `BeDomNode.element` overload-collision defect:
# two co-compiled `static fn element` definitions with differing arity
# corrupted every subsequently constructed/stored BeDomNode's struct
# fields under JIT (a tag_name/id_attr/style_attr read off any
# element-shaped node came back empty), while the interpreter read the
# identical tree correctly. Root-caused with an isolated, tokenizer-free
# repro -- see doc/08_tracking/bug/jit_run_file_pipeline_gaps_2026-07-30.md
# section 16.2. Fixed by renaming the rare 2-arg overload to
# `element_with_id`, leaving the ~250-call-site 1-arg form as `element`.
use std.gc_async_mut.gpu.browser_engine.dom.{be_dom_debug_manual_tree_dump}

fn main():
    print be_dom_debug_manual_tree_dump()
